  "lineage": "The post-1950s folk-club and festival performance form of maritime song, shaped in Britain by A.L. Lloyd and Ewan MacColl's 1956 Blow Boys Blow, by Stan Hugill's residencies at the Falmouth and Mystic Seaport shanty festivals from the 1970s, and by the Fisherman's Friends and Sea Shanty TikTok waves of 2010 and 2021; performed at fixed brisk tempos in strophic verse-and-chorus form with strong unison male chorus on the refrain, frequently with concertina, melodeon, fiddle or guitar accompaniment that the working original never had.",
